# Phase 4 — Firewall & Security Rules

## Practical Commands

The following command was used to inspect the current `iptables` firewall configuration on Kali Linux.

### 1. Inspect the `iptables` Firewall Configuration

```bash
# Inspect the current iptables firewall configuration
# -L: List the firewall rules
# -n: Display IP addresses and ports numerically
# -v: Display detailed information and packet/byte counters
sudo iptables -L -n -v
```

### 2. Firewall Chains

The command displays the main firewall chains:

```text
INPUT    → Traffic entering the system
FORWARD  → Traffic passing through the system
OUTPUT   → Traffic leaving the system
```

### 3. Default Firewall Policies

The command also shows the default policy of each chain.

In this practical test:

```text
INPUT policy:   ACCEPT
FORWARD policy: ACCEPT
OUTPUT policy:  ACCEPT
```

### 4. Firewall Rules and Counters

No visible filtering rules were configured during this practical test.

The packet and byte counters were:

```text
Packet counters: 0
Byte counters:   0
```

This indicated that no visible `iptables` filtering rules had processed traffic during the check.

